WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.303
I moderated a panel this week

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.804
packed with heavy hitters

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:05.905
Avril Haines,

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:06.339
the US

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.341
director of National Intelligence,

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.176
the secretary general of NATO's

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.611
Jens Stoltenberg,

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.446
President Duda of Poland,

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.015
and the deputy prime ministers

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:15.682
of Ukraine

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:16.716
and Canada,

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:19.219
Julius Danko and Chrystia Freeland.

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.955
I started with a question to MS. Haines.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.456
I wanted to know the U.S.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.658
intelligence community's perspective

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.694
on where the war is now

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.496
and where it's headed

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.530
The way we would say

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.232
it is not a stalemate, but

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:34.200
but really a grinding conflict

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.068
at this stage

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:37.237
where quite literally we're talking

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.972
about hundreds of meters

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.040
being fought over

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.008
in the context of the front lines.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.444
But I think from our perspective,

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.713
both militaries

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.181
obviously have challenges.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.417
It will be extremely important

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:51.618
for Ukraine

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:52.685
to receive

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.421
essentially military assistance

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:57.257
and economic assistance moving forward

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.391
in order for them

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.293
to be able to continue to manage

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.762
what they have been heroically doing.

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.431
And on the Russian side,

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:06.666
we see also significant challenges

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:08.802
and munitions

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:12.472
supplies, morale, exhaustion,

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:15.442
some dysfunction in the leadership

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:17.043
and so on, things that are,

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.678
I think, making it more difficult

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.581
for the Russian military as well

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.250
to do that.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.485
It is striking to me

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:28.588
how strong the West has been

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:29.923
in other parts

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.291
of the world as well

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.960
in supporting Ukraine.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.229
Do you think that the response is

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.099
strong enough and more importantly,

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:40.700
what everybody worries

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.136
about is it will it stay strong,

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.773
this assistance?

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.375
We've just sent to two to two.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.878
Ukraine is still not enough

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.917
Ukraine needs more our efforts.

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:01.921
It's more our aid.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.390
And we should mobilize ourselves

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:08.161
to help them because it's the situation

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:11.097
is it's really difficult

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:15.235
and I'm afraid

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:16.469
now it is.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.738
And it will be in a few,

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.841
maybe months, maybe weeks.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.476
The crucial moment

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.512
next, crucial moments of this war

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.780
and and

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.950
this moment will answer for the question

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:34.454
Will Ukraine

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:36.689
survive or not?

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:38.858
Chrystia,

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.027
do you worry about the staying

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:42.829
power of the West

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.835
So the short answer is,

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.003
of course,

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:52.572
it would be stupid and naive not to

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:57.110
but I think we're going to do it.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:00.747
And I think, you know, of course I worry.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.850
I am ultimately extremely confident

00:03:04.551 --> 00:03:06.219
and I am extremely confident

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.921
first and foremost

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:10.790
because of the magnificent,

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:14.093
magnificent job Ukraine is doing.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.962
And as President Zelensky

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.031
very crucially pointed out,

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.133
supplying Ukraine with the money

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.302
it needs to win the war

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:25.572
is ultimately in our own self-interest.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.141
So I'm a finance minister.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:32.345
And if you were to say to me,

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:37.317
what is the one thing that G7

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:40.019
finance ministers, G7 governments

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.854
this year could do?

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:44.490
That's actually in our power, right?

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.025
We don't control COVID.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:48.161
We don't control global supply chains.

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:49.262
We don't control

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:50.763
whether there will be immaculate

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:53.032
disinflation or not.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:53.733
One thing

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.367
where we have

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:57.570
some real practical levers is

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:58.771
we can help

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:02.575
Ukraine when clearly, definitively

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:06.045
and if we do that, if that happens

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:08.214
this year,

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:09.749
you know it as well as I do, Fareed.

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.818
That would be a huge boost

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.387
to the global economy.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:14.687
Mr.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:15.488
Secretary General,

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:16.222
you heard

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.490
the president of Ukraine say

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.993
he would like to be a member of NATO.

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:20.860
Will you let him in

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.064
NATO's position remains unchanged,

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:25.765
and that is that

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:28.501
the Ukraine will become a member of NATO.

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:31.004
Then, of course, the main focus now

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:31.938
is to support

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:32.605
Ukraine

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.907
to ensure that Ukraine wins the war

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:35.908
and prevails

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.343
as a sovereign, independent,

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.646
democratic nation in Europe.

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.447
It is extremely important

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:42.649
that President Putin doesn't

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:43.850
win this war,

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.785
partly because it would be a tragedy

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:47.020
for the Ukrainians,

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.588
but would be very dangerous

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:50.156
for all of us,

00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:51.291
because then the message

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:52.625
to authoritarian leaders,

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:53.760
not only to Putin,

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.962
but also other authoritarian leaders,

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.064
is that when they use brutal force,

00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:59.966
when they violate international law,

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:02.502
they achieve what they want.

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:03.836
And that will be a very bad

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.338
and dangerous lessons.

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:07.307
It will make the world more dangerous

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:09.275
and more vulnerable.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:10.343
And that is reason why

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:12.078
if we want

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:12.812
a negotiated,

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:13.713
peaceful solution

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:14.814
to the war in Ukraine,

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:16.716
we need to provide military support

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:17.517
to Ukraine.

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.218
That's the only way

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:20.820
weapons

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.823
they are the way to peace.

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:24.791
And and

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:26.759
and that may sound like a paradox

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:27.660
about the

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.462
but the only way to have a negotiated

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:31.698
agreement is to convince President

00:05:31.698 --> 00:05:32.965
Putin that they will not win

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:33.766
on the battlefield.

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:36.903
He has to sit down and and negotiate.

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:39.906
Nobody knows how this war will end.

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:41.040
Most likely

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.376
it will end around the negotiating table.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.045
What what we do know is that what happens

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:47.013
happens around

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.781
that negotiating table

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:50.049
is totally dependent

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:51.651
on the strength of the battlefield.

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:53.419
And if we want Ukraine to prevail,

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:56.089
then they need the military strength.

